  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "As someone who flies DJI drones, I would love to see functionality for motion controls similarly to the DJI Avata series for the VrChat drone. The DJI Avata drones use a one handed controller that uses its tilt to control the drone. An analogue stick in the front that you pull or push for forward and backwards, tilting to turn the drone in any direction, and a joystick for various controls like quick acro or sideways motion. \n\nThe Quest controllers are more than capable of performing these kinda of actions for the VrChat drone, but a couple of the actions may need use of the other controller. This control method is very fun to use and is great for racing and stunts. \n\nHere is a video on the DJI Avata: https://youtu.be/RNhmV4yCP6M?si=GUqnwfUJbNDrlj_M",
